---
title: Andaa Salan
description: this is a basic egg curry that is made at home. My son loves it and if you have the ingredients it really is a less than 30 min recipe
---

Boil @egg{2} and @potato{1} in a #pot.

Measure out @fried onion{1%tablespoon}, @garlic paste{1%teaspoon}, @ginger paste{1%teaspoon}, @red chili powder{1/2%teaspoon}, @turmeric{1/2%teaspoon}, @ground cumin{1/2%teaspoon}, and @ground coriander{1/2%teaspoon}.

Add everything to a #pan and cook until the individual scents disappear and khushboo (good smell) comes, ~{10-15%minutes}. Add @water{} as needed so it doesn't burn and @oil{} as needed so it fries. Add @salt{} to taste and stir frequently.

Add @tomato sauce{1/2%cup} and cook for ~{5-10%minutes} until the tomato has cooked out. Add @oil{} as needed.

Add around @water{1/2%cup} and cook for ~{5%minutes}.

Cut the boiled @egg{} and @potato{} and add into the salan. Mix and turn off the heat. Add @salt{} to taste.
